% approach would be to consider the rod and end mass explicitly. In that
% case, the weight of the system could be considered to be located at the
% system's mass center $l_G = (Ml+0.5ml))/(M+m)$. In that case, the mass
% moment of inertia is $I_O = ml^2/3 + Ml^2$. Depending on the parameters
% of your particular pendulum, you can assess if this added fidelity is
