% The potentiometer, which is physically attached to the rod of the
% pendulum (not shown), is connected to the Arduino board as shown. The
% potentiometer is used for sensing the pendulum's angular position and the
% Arduino board is simply employed to power the sensor, to acquire the
% data, and to communicate the data to Simulink. Specifically, the power
% and ground from the Arduino board are connected to the outermost pins of
% the potentiometer. The middle pin is the potentiometer's "output" and is
